I replaced the linear scan with a lazily-built direct-index lookup table (65536 entries, one per FIT_UINT16 message number), built once and iterated backwards so duplicate numbers still resolve to the first match; each call becomes a single O(1) array index plus the cheap static-init guard.

```include
#include <array>
```

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const std::array<const MESG*, 65536> table = [] {
        std::array<const MESG*, 65536> t{};
        for (int i = MESGS - 1; i >= 0; --i)
            t[mesgs[i].num] = &mesgs[i];
        return t;
    }();

    return table[num];
}
```